  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Gulfstream Aerospace recorded $313M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, with 79 awards and an average award size of $4M. Obligations are up 134.8% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows fluctuations in obligations: Gulfstream Aerospace obligated $206M in FY21, $115M in FY22, $119M in FY23, $225M in FY24, and $133M in FY25. The Department of Homeland Security and the Department of Defense are the largest buyers in FY2026 to date, with $185M and $126M in obligations respectively. Commercial Air, Rail, and Water Transportation Equipment Rental and Leasing is the largest NAICS market with $188M, followed by Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $101M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $24.8M. Smaller NAICS markets include Software Publishers at $140K and All Other Publishers at $67.2K. Current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity. Use the agency and market concentrations above to focus outreach and capture planning for the remainder of the fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Gulfstream Aerospace obligations by agency?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is the top buyer with $185M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense follows with $126M. Other agency buyers in FY2026 to date include the Department of Justice at $2.1M, NASA at $146K, and the Department of Transportation at $45.6K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which product and service markets drive Gulfstream Aerospace federal revenue?",
        "body": "Commercial Air, Rail, and Water Transportation Equipment Rental and Leasing is the largest NAICS market with $188M in FY2026 to date. Other Support Activities for Air Transportation contributed $101M and Aircraft Manufacturing contributed $24.8M. Smaller markets include Software Publishers at $140K and All Other Publishers at $67.2K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Gulfstream Aerospace make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Gulfstream Aerospace has $313M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Gulfstream Aerospace received 79 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4M, and obligations are up 134.8% year over year. Historical annual obligations include $206M in FY21, $115M in FY22, $119M in FY23, $225M in FY24, and $133M in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Gulfstream Aerospace?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security is the top buyer of Gulfstream Aerospace in FY2026 to date, with $185M in obligations. The Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer with $126M. Other agencies buying from Gulfstream Aerospace in FY2026 to date include the Department of Justice at $2.1M, NASA at $146K, and the Department of Transportation at $45.6K."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Gulfstream Aerospace sell to the government?",
      "a": "Gulfstream Aerospace sells products and services concentrated in transportation and aviation support markets. Commercial Air, Rail, and Water Transportation Equipment Rental and Leasing is the largest NAICS market for Gulfstream Aerospace at $188M in FY2026 to date. Gulfstream Aerospace also sells Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $101M and Aircraft Manufacturing at $24.8M, with smaller activity in Software Publishers ($140K) and All Other Publishers ($67.2K)."
    },
